Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 44 CLINICAL DATA  Microcalcifications on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  FOCALLY CRIBRIFORM TYPE  CLOSE TO AN INKED MARGIN  WITH SEVERELY ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA INVOLVING MULTIPLE LOBULES  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FOCAL MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 53 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The atypical cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The atypical cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Intraductal carcinoma cannot be recognized in the sections stained for hormone receptor proteins  One can see atypical ductal cells  however  and they show the same cytological characteristics as the cells that comprise the ductal carcinoma in situ  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 47 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab labeled with the patient s named and unit number is a 2 0cm in diameter round  pink tan fragment of tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal bands of tan tissue surrounded by fat  A needle localizing wire is placed  There is no frozen section done  An accompanying x ray shows calcifications adjacent to the thick segment of the localization wire  Specimen is submitted entirely in A through E  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS RIGHT BREAST   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , ADH_DCIS.
